1
00:01:43,810 --> 00:01:47,700
[KING OF COMEDY]

2
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:50,950
[Episode 7]

3
00:01:52,430 --> 00:01:55,620
♪ Lost in the crowds, we carry on ♪

4
00:01:52,789 --> 00:01:53,470
Anyway...

5
00:01:54,590 --> 00:01:55,920
as for making movies,

6
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:59,140
♪ Someone will stay
with you through day and night ♪

7
00:01:56,590 --> 00:01:57,310
you guys...

8
00:01:58,000 --> 00:01:58,789
I'll be the director.

9
00:01:59,530 --> 00:02:02,850
♪ The art of loving and being loved ♪

10
00:02:01,230 --> 00:02:02,150
You be the director?

11
00:02:03,470 --> 00:02:07,070
♪ I'll give my all
to get it right for you ♪

12
00:02:04,150 --> 00:02:04,840
Do you know how to do it?

13
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:05,350
No.

14
00:02:05,950 --> 00:02:06,590
Then how are you gonna direct?

15
00:02:06,950 --> 00:02:07,950
Aren't you here?

16
00:02:08,330 --> 00:02:11,570
♪ Who would risk it all for you? ♪

17
00:02:11,970 --> 00:02:15,150
♪ Locking all the sorrow deep inside ♪

18
00:02:12,870 --> 00:02:15,000
Am I?

19
00:02:15,570 --> 00:02:19,310
♪ Like a clown who can become ♪

20
00:02:15,750 --> 00:02:17,030
Haven't you always been here?

21
00:02:20,070 --> 00:02:23,930
♪ The superhero who makes you smile ♪

22
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,150
I left for a day.

23
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:27,820
♪ Oh, time ♪

24
00:02:27,850 --> 00:02:31,650
♪ People who live like clowns ♪

25
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:29,630
I believe you'll help me.

26
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:30,800
Let's go!

27
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:34,820
♪ Have long forgotten the dust
on their sleeves ♪

28
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:34,800
Oh, right!

29
00:02:34,990 --> 00:02:40,320
♪ With honest hearts,
we make this world more tender ♪

30
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:37,190
That dog died of old age.

31
00:02:40,350 --> 00:02:43,829
♪ Oh, time ♪

32
00:02:44,180 --> 00:02:48,160
♪ We who were once loved by clowns ♪

33
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:53,150
Busy?

34
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:54,840
Junnan.

35
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:04,750
Busy?

36
00:03:05,150 --> 00:03:05,630
Noodles are here?

37
00:03:05,630 --> 00:03:06,240
Yeah.

38
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:06,750
Put them there.

39
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:09,710
I'm looking for Mr. Gao.

40
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:11,870
-Mr. Gao.
-Jiaoqi!

41
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:13,000
Jiaoqi!

42
00:03:13,710 --> 00:03:14,430
-Your noodles are here.
-Mr. Chen.

43
00:03:16,150 --> 00:03:17,070
Eat while it's hot.

44
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:18,870
How did you sleep last night?

45
00:03:20,030 --> 00:03:20,750
Pretty well.

46
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:22,590
It's just that the AC

47
00:03:22,590 --> 00:03:23,400
was a bit too strong.

48
00:03:23,470 --> 00:03:24,430
I almost caught a cold.

49
00:03:25,910 --> 00:03:27,360
Then don't turn it on.

50
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:28,840
Besides,

51
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:31,190
your vehicle is using our electricity.

52
00:03:31,910 --> 00:03:33,070
That number goes up really fast.

53
00:03:33,490 --> 00:03:35,150
Come on. We're already trying to conserve
as much as we can.

54
00:03:35,150 --> 00:03:36,710
We didn't even dare
to turn on all the lights.

55
00:03:36,710 --> 00:03:37,030
See?

56
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:40,070
Atmosphere.

57
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:41,840
It's fine.

58
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:42,840
The electricity bill isn't much.

59
00:03:42,910 --> 00:03:43,750
I'll reimburse you later.

60
00:03:44,310 --> 00:03:45,120
That's good.

61
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:47,040
When is later?

62
00:03:50,150 --> 00:03:51,680
Aren't we preparing
to tackle them one by one?

63
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:53,829
I asked you to prepare
the villager roster.

64
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:54,630
Did you prepare it?

65
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:55,240
I did.

66
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:56,910
I'll give it to you later.

67
00:03:58,590 --> 00:03:59,960
Should we set the AC to heat?

68
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:01,520
Open the freezer door.

69
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:02,520
Let the cold and hot air clash.

70
00:04:03,030 --> 00:04:03,750
Stir it up a bit.

71
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:05,470
Let the air circulate and...

72
00:04:05,470 --> 00:04:06,150
Alright, alright.

73
00:04:19,870 --> 00:04:20,560
I can't see it clearly.

74
00:04:35,750 --> 00:04:36,480
What are you waiting for?

75
00:04:42,909 --> 00:04:44,270
Give me the money for the noodles.

76
00:04:47,630 --> 00:04:48,390
I'll give it to you later.

77
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:53,150
Okay.

78
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:54,750
Just kidding. My treat.

79
00:04:55,750 --> 00:04:56,360
Take your time.

80
00:04:59,460 --> 00:05:00,330
That's yours too.

81
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:18,000
So you two are determined

82
00:05:18,190 --> 00:05:20,190
to make it a sure thing

83
00:05:20,870 --> 00:05:23,430
and shoot this movie, right?

84
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:25,630
Okay.

85
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:29,360
Since Zhou Ke
isn't participating in the movie,

86
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:31,660
how about we just leave first?

87
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:36,820
Let's give Mr. Zhou some time.

88
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:37,870
I believe in him.

89
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:38,520
Right.

90
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,800
We came to talk to you today

91
00:05:42,430 --> 00:05:43,560
because we

92
00:05:44,150 --> 00:05:46,720
have a question to ask you.

93
00:05:47,190 --> 00:05:49,600
After all, in this field, you are

94
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:51,310
the most professional,

95
00:05:52,510 --> 00:05:53,830
the most influential...

96
00:05:54,150 --> 00:05:54,390
Come on.

97
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:56,250
And the most authoritative...

98
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:57,040
Well, I...

99
00:05:58,150 --> 00:05:58,600
One.

100
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:02,270
We want to know

101
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:03,870
how much it would cost

102
00:06:04,390 --> 00:06:06,720
to make a movie.

103
00:06:07,190 --> 00:06:08,120
That's hard to say.

104
00:06:08,630 --> 00:06:11,360
It mainly depends
on the cast, crew, and production.

105
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:12,750
It can cost any amount.

106
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:15,160
What about a good one?

107
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:17,970
Like the ones we've participated in...

108
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,360
About 300 million.

109
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:27,630
What about the ones
you never participated in,

110
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:29,110
the more ordinary ones?

111
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:30,480
30 million.

112
00:06:33,050 --> 00:06:34,130
Can we do it with 30,000?

113
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:36,080
Time to sleep.

114
00:06:37,950 --> 00:06:40,090
We only have 9,000 right now.

115
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:40,950
Can we do it?

116
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:44,190
You can't.

117
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:46,830
Think about
how expensive it is to make a movie.

118
00:06:46,830 --> 00:06:48,190
Lighting, camera, art, makeup, props,

119
00:06:48,190 --> 00:06:49,120
food, drink, and accommodation—

120
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:50,360
isn't all that going to cost money?

121
00:06:50,390 --> 00:06:51,390
You only have 9,000...

122
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:53,720
Just 9,000?

123
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:55,360
Then the labor fee
you promised us before...

124
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:55,870
No, no, no.

125
00:06:55,870 --> 00:06:57,600
Your share has been set aside.

126
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:58,750
It's not included in this.

127
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:00,120
You scared me.

128
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:05,190
I was... just asking.

129
00:07:05,270 --> 00:07:05,750
Understand.

130
00:07:06,510 --> 00:07:08,190
So now...

131
00:07:08,190 --> 00:07:10,160
as long as we have 30,000,
we can do it, right?

132
00:07:14,750 --> 00:07:16,700
Most likely...

133
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:17,430
maybe.

134
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:18,560
Okay!

135
00:07:19,830 --> 00:07:21,630
My brother and I will work hard!

136
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:25,070
How do you plan to work hard?

137
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:28,680
We'll crowdfund the movie

138
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:30,190
by getting the villagers

139
00:07:30,630 --> 00:07:31,480
to invest in it.

140
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:32,630
We'll promise them a share of the profits!

141
00:07:34,150 --> 00:07:35,920
You ended up on this path anyway.

142
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:38,860
Crowdfund?
You think you can get the money?

143
00:07:40,870 --> 00:07:42,560
You underestimate us too much.

144
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:08,870
For this fundraising,

145
00:08:09,510 --> 00:08:12,160
I'll handle Yudan, Shengzai,
Zuxian, Qingxia,

146
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:13,730
Haonan, Chaowei, and Jiahui.

147
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:14,360
Yes!

148
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:16,630
And you will handle Chen Langbiao,
Mr. Chenpi,

149
00:08:16,630 --> 00:08:18,600
Mr. Shark, Ms. Haigou, Mr. Haixing,

150
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:20,310
Mr. Xianyu, Ms. Zicai, and Sangbiao!

151
00:08:20,310 --> 00:08:21,000
Yes!

152
00:08:22,310 --> 00:08:22,720
Sister,

153
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:25,060
can you give me two easier ones to handle?

154
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:27,240
If you can't even
overcome this little difficulty,

155
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:28,680
how can you be the village chief?

156
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,320
Let's start warming up!

157
00:08:38,549 --> 00:08:39,870
Warm-up complete!

158
00:08:40,630 --> 00:08:41,600
Target: 20,000!

159
00:08:42,010 --> 00:08:42,809
Giddy up!

160
00:08:56,610 --> 00:08:57,540
[Give us some money]

161
00:08:57,990 --> 00:08:59,560
[Please]

162
00:09:01,010 --> 00:09:01,500
[Give us money]

163
00:09:02,450 --> 00:09:03,180
[Give us money]

164
00:09:11,980 --> 00:09:12,740
[Yeah]

165
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:15,600
[Ummmm]

166
00:09:15,980 --> 00:09:17,700
[Please have mercy]

167
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,170
[Give whatever you can]

168
00:09:19,380 --> 00:09:20,330
[Take pity on me]

169
00:09:20,580 --> 00:09:21,240
[Give us some money]

170
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:22,660
[Even a dime or two is fine]

171
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:24,860
[Don't go! Give us some more]

172
00:09:25,030 --> 00:09:25,500
[Broadcasting Station]

173
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:31,670
Villagers, invest in our movie!

174
00:09:31,670 --> 00:09:33,030
Now you can invest in our movie.

175
00:09:33,150 --> 00:09:34,390
Then we can develop
better cultural tourism!

176
00:09:34,390 --> 00:09:35,150
And we can make big money!

177
00:09:35,150 --> 00:09:35,630
Sister.

178
00:09:36,130 --> 00:09:37,730
Brother, how is it going?

179
00:09:39,390 --> 00:09:39,910
And you?

180
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:43,910
My knees are almost swollen with fluid.

181
00:09:44,390 --> 00:09:46,360
My throat is killing me.

182
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:48,960
I feel like no one

183
00:09:48,960 --> 00:09:50,940
really believes in

184
00:09:51,630 --> 00:09:53,030
investing in a movie.

185
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:56,750
Even all my unique skills
failed to impress them.

186
00:09:57,150 --> 00:09:58,270
And today, I even had Ms. Haigou

187
00:09:58,270 --> 00:09:59,760
run over my foot
with her electric scooter for nothing.

188
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:02,840
-Electric scooter?
-She ran over my foot.

189
00:10:03,510 --> 00:10:03,750
Brother,

190
00:10:04,910 --> 00:10:05,750
have you noticed that

191
00:10:05,750 --> 00:10:07,080
every household

192
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:08,960
has a new electric scooter outside?

193
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:13,630
Yeah.

194
00:10:21,730 --> 00:10:22,890
Where did they get them?

195
00:10:22,920 --> 00:10:24,000
Do we have one?

196
00:10:24,750 --> 00:10:25,720
Is that the point?

197
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:26,600
Let's go.

198
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:27,720
We need to

199
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:28,720
go find Mr. Maling now.

200
00:10:28,740 --> 00:10:29,710
He will definitely help us.

201
00:10:29,790 --> 00:10:30,780
Right. Let's go.

202
00:10:30,870 --> 00:10:31,480
Wait for me.

203
00:10:32,270 --> 00:10:33,550
This old man is really weird.

204
00:10:33,740 --> 00:10:34,460
Exactly.

205
00:10:34,870 --> 00:10:35,600
If he doesn't agree to the demolition,

206
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:36,670
why did he make us
carry the scooter up here?

207
00:10:36,670 --> 00:10:37,320
Seriously.

208
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:38,430
My back is already bad.

209
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:40,230
How many scooters did we give out today?

210
00:10:40,630 --> 00:10:41,910
A dozen, I think.

211
00:10:42,460 --> 00:10:43,120
A dozen?

212
00:10:44,710 --> 00:10:45,440
It's you!

213
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:46,670
Fei!

214
00:10:47,910 --> 00:10:49,030
-So what if it's us?
-Run!

215
00:10:49,030 --> 00:10:50,030
Run? Why should we run?

216
00:10:50,550 --> 00:10:50,870
Wait!

217
00:10:51,250 --> 00:10:51,700
Don't!

218
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:52,510
-Fei!
-Wait!

219
00:10:54,390 --> 00:10:56,080
Fei! Gao Jiaoqi!

220
00:10:56,100 --> 00:10:57,460
Stop it. I haven't got on the scooter yet!

221
00:10:59,910 --> 00:11:01,080
I knew it was them!

222
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:01,870
That scooter...

223
00:11:03,060 --> 00:11:04,660
Come on. Let's go find Mr. Maling.

224
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:08,720
Mr. Maling!

225
00:11:08,870 --> 00:11:09,790
Mr. Maling!

226
00:11:09,910 --> 00:11:11,200
Mr. Maling!

227
00:11:11,270 --> 00:11:12,080
Mr. Maling!

228
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:13,440
Zhen, Jiahao.

229
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:14,510
You didn't agree to the demolition,
did you?

230
00:11:15,150 --> 00:11:15,960
Demolition?

231
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:18,240
Of course I didn't

232
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,440
agree to the demolition.

233
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:20,790
If they do the demolition,

234
00:11:20,790 --> 00:11:22,670
I won't be able to find the treasure.

235
00:11:22,670 --> 00:11:23,270
That's good.

236
00:11:23,290 --> 00:11:24,840
Great. Well, Mr. Maling,

237
00:11:25,010 --> 00:11:25,960
can we talk about

238
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:27,750
investing in the movie?

239
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Let's sit down and talk.

240
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:52,200
Impressive.

241
00:11:52,460 --> 00:11:53,300
Mr. Maling,

242
00:11:53,390 --> 00:11:55,390
your moving castle
has been upgraded again?

243
00:11:57,480 --> 00:11:58,200
Last month,

244
00:11:58,200 --> 00:11:59,750
a motorcade came from Harbin.

245
00:11:59,870 --> 00:12:00,910
I repaired their cars.

246
00:12:01,150 --> 00:12:02,150
One of them

247
00:12:02,150 --> 00:12:03,200
gave me a large sum of money.

248
00:12:03,730 --> 00:12:05,690
I used this money
to upgrade my moving castle.

249
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:06,960
Now I call it

250
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:08,790
Harbin's Moving Castle.

251
00:12:09,440 --> 00:12:10,000
That's great.

252
00:12:10,280 --> 00:12:11,360
So do you have money

253
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:12,930
to invest in our movie?

254
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:13,550
Of course.

255
00:12:14,390 --> 00:12:15,030
Last month,

256
00:12:15,240 --> 00:12:16,480
a motorcade came from Harbin.

257
00:12:16,510 --> 00:12:17,390
I repaired their cars.

258
00:12:17,840 --> 00:12:19,390
One of them gave me a large sum of money.

259
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:21,390
I used this money

260
00:12:21,670 --> 00:12:23,440
to transform my moving castle into

261
00:12:23,670 --> 00:12:25,240
Harbin's Moving Castle.

262
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:26,790
That's great.

263
00:12:26,910 --> 00:12:27,360
Perfect timing.

264
00:12:27,390 --> 00:12:28,870
Are you interested in our new movie?

265
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:30,240
I put this large sum of money

266
00:12:30,390 --> 00:12:31,840
into my Harbin's Moving Castle.

267
00:12:33,930 --> 00:12:34,830
You used all the money?

268
00:12:36,910 --> 00:12:38,120
As I just said,

269
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:40,030
a motorcade came from Harbin...

270
00:12:40,030 --> 00:12:40,510
Alright.

271
00:12:40,510 --> 00:12:41,440
Mr. Maling, I get it.

272
00:12:42,270 --> 00:12:43,510
So you have no money now?

273
00:12:46,010 --> 00:12:47,670
I have more and more equipment now.

274
00:12:47,840 --> 00:12:49,080
When I find the treasure,

275
00:12:49,270 --> 00:12:50,720
I can invest a large sum of money in you.

276
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:51,720
It will be soon.

277
00:12:53,010 --> 00:12:54,460
How long will that take?

278
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:57,360
Well then, Mr. Maling, get some rest.

279
00:12:57,550 --> 00:12:58,840
We'll go ask others.

280
00:13:01,270 --> 00:13:01,790
Jiahao.

281
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:04,240
If you have extra dry rations at home,

282
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:05,480
bring some for me.

283
00:13:06,630 --> 00:13:07,960
I haven't been sleeping well lately.

284
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:09,670
I'm groggy and hungry.

285
00:13:10,630 --> 00:13:12,390
Then we'll go back
and bring you some fish balls.

286
00:13:12,630 --> 00:13:13,320
Okay.

287
00:13:15,790 --> 00:13:16,670
Zhen, Jiahao.

288
00:13:17,390 --> 00:13:19,910
If you want to make a movie,

289
00:13:20,670 --> 00:13:23,270
I can provide some technical support.

290
00:13:24,510 --> 00:13:25,720
Although we went to so many houses

291
00:13:25,750 --> 00:13:26,870
and didn't raise a single cent,

292
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:28,480
we did recruit a person.

293
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:30,510
Let's welcome Mr. Maling to the team.

294
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:34,580
Let's not be too optimistic right now.

295
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:36,840
We're literally facing problems
both internally and externally.

296
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:37,790
I'll make two points.

297
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:38,550
First,

298
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:40,120
now, the villagers

299
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:41,750
don't believe we can make a movie at all,

300
00:13:42,030 --> 00:13:43,190
so they don't dare to invest.

301
00:13:43,510 --> 00:13:43,720
Yes.

302
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:44,120
Second,

303
00:13:44,630 --> 00:13:45,750
Gao Jiaoqi and Fei

304
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,320
are giving away electric scooters
door to door.

305
00:13:47,630 --> 00:13:48,840
Isn't this just causing trouble for us?

306
00:13:49,030 --> 00:13:49,720
If this continues,

307
00:13:50,270 --> 00:13:50,910
we are done for.

308
00:13:51,360 --> 00:13:51,750
So,

309
00:13:51,750 --> 00:13:53,910
we need to do something big now

310
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:54,840
to let them know

311
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:56,440
that we are serious about making a movie.

312
00:13:56,680 --> 00:13:57,600
Otherwise, if we keep waiting,

313
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:59,390
the villagers will be less likely
to believe us.

314
00:13:59,510 --> 00:13:59,910
Okay.

315
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:01,870
The key is that we don't have a script.

316
00:14:02,150 --> 00:14:02,840
What are we going to shoot?

317
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:03,720
It's fine.

318
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:05,240
It doesn't matter.

319
00:14:05,510 --> 00:14:06,720
We can shoot
some establishing shots first.

320
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:10,440
What are establishing shots?

321
00:14:10,510 --> 00:14:11,720
As its name implies,

322
00:14:11,910 --> 00:14:13,790
it's a shot with no people,
used to establish the setting—

323
00:14:13,910 --> 00:14:14,910
just the surroundings,
flowers, plants, things like that.

324
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:16,270
If there are no people,

325
00:14:16,270 --> 00:14:17,320
how can we make it big?

326
00:14:17,750 --> 00:14:19,670
We can make a big scene when we shoot.

327
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:22,240
Make it look grand and spectacular.

328
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:23,870
How do we do it?

329
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:26,240
We can do aerial filming.

330
00:14:28,130 --> 00:14:29,480
Right, we can do aerial filming.

331
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:30,530
That's a good idea.

332
00:14:30,920 --> 00:14:31,830
What is aerial filming?

333
00:14:33,550 --> 00:14:34,480
Aerial filming

334
00:14:34,480 --> 00:14:35,550
is exactly what it sounds like.

335
00:14:35,580 --> 00:14:37,340
Aviation! Shooting from the sky.

336
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:38,520
Shooting from the sky?

337
00:14:42,440 --> 00:14:43,670
But we don't have the equipment.

338
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:52,050
This is my flying fortress.

339
00:14:58,270 --> 00:14:59,390
Can this fly?

340
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:05,390
How much of a scene can this make?

341
00:15:08,820 --> 00:15:11,110
[Ten Tips for Directors:
1. Stay true to yourself.]

342
00:15:11,110 --> 00:15:13,400
[2. Listen to other people's advice.
3. Don't shoot big scenes! Don't ever do it!]

343
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:23,800
Ke.

344
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:25,510
Is this little snowman...

345
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:28,080
What are you doing?

346
00:15:30,480 --> 00:15:31,030
Writing a diary.

347
00:15:31,790 --> 00:15:32,790
I've known you for over 20 years.

348
00:15:32,790 --> 00:15:33,960
How many words have you written in total?

349
00:15:36,630 --> 00:15:37,270
They are preparing.

350
00:15:37,270 --> 00:15:37,870
Aren't you going?

351
00:15:38,550 --> 00:15:39,190
No.

352
00:15:39,870 --> 00:15:41,030
If you're not going, I'll go.

353
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:42,120
I have to go.

354
00:15:43,270 --> 00:15:43,910
Then I'm going.

355
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:44,790
Go ahead.

356
00:15:49,120 --> 00:15:49,790
Are you really not going?

357
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:50,870
Why would I go?

358
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:55,080
Then I'll go by myself.

359
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:58,000
Keep writing.

360
00:15:58,360 --> 00:15:59,910
Do you know how to spell the word "diary?"

361
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:02,360
D-I-A-R-Y.

362
00:16:06,160 --> 00:16:07,040
Don't go.

363
00:16:14,870 --> 00:16:16,200
This is my flying fortress.

364
00:16:16,790 --> 00:16:18,820
It's made of the chief's security camera,

365
00:16:18,870 --> 00:16:19,840
the chief's clothes,

366
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:21,120
the chief's curtains,

367
00:16:21,270 --> 00:16:22,550
and the chief's rope.

368
00:16:23,150 --> 00:16:24,240
I affectionately call it

369
00:16:24,840 --> 00:16:25,510
Mr. Hug.

370
00:16:25,870 --> 00:16:27,440
You should call it Mr. Chief.

371
00:16:27,770 --> 00:16:29,060
The monitor connected to it

372
00:16:29,510 --> 00:16:30,390
will transfer the aerial footage

373
00:16:30,390 --> 00:16:31,840
to my phone in real time.

374
00:16:32,270 --> 00:16:33,200
Is it reliable?

375
00:16:33,380 --> 00:16:33,940
Yes.

376
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:35,000
Six years ago,

377
00:16:35,550 --> 00:16:37,030
I rode it around the world.

378
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:38,240
Around the world?

379
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:39,150
You traveled around the world?

380
00:16:39,670 --> 00:16:40,600
It exploded as soon as I left the village.

381
00:16:40,950 --> 00:16:42,120
Isn't that unreliable?

382
00:16:42,650 --> 00:16:44,530
Every time it exploded,

383
00:16:44,790 --> 00:16:47,480
I patched it up.

384
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:49,200
There isn't a single piece

385
00:16:49,200 --> 00:16:50,360
of the original fabric left.

386
00:16:50,870 --> 00:16:52,120
We can call it the Balloon of Theseus.

387
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:53,360
Every time it exploded, you patched it up?

388
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:54,600
How many times have you fallen?

389
00:16:55,030 --> 00:16:57,120
Mr. Maling,
you can actually leave the village by car.

390
00:16:57,330 --> 00:16:58,140
Riding this thing?

391
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:00,870
It's a miracle you've survived this long.

392
00:17:01,240 --> 00:17:03,000
The unoccupied version is 100% reliable.

393
00:17:03,510 --> 00:17:04,680
It won't get anyone hurt.

394
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:06,640
Come on.

395
00:17:07,069 --> 00:17:07,640
Come on.

396
00:17:07,750 --> 00:17:09,680
Three, two, one.

397
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:10,640
Let go.

398
00:17:11,310 --> 00:17:12,030
Go!

399
00:17:12,030 --> 00:17:13,000
-Gosh!
-Theseus!

400
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,680
It was so heavy.
It almost dragged me away.

401
00:17:16,030 --> 00:17:16,680
Mr. Maling,

402
00:17:17,030 --> 00:17:19,680
how do we get this back
after the aerial filming?

403
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:20,920
We don't.

404
00:17:22,550 --> 00:17:24,400
When it completes the mission
given by humans,

405
00:17:24,599 --> 00:17:26,160
it should go where it wants to go.

406
00:17:34,510 --> 00:17:36,510
Making movies really burns money.

407
00:17:36,870 --> 00:17:38,220
Mr. Zhou would definitely be very happy

408
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:39,780
if he saw this.

409
00:17:40,720 --> 00:17:41,900
I wonder where he is now.

410
00:17:44,510 --> 00:17:45,030
Help!

411
00:17:47,110 --> 00:17:48,640
Isn't Mr. Zhou right there?

412
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:51,350
It's getting higher and higher!

413
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:52,110
Ke!

414
00:17:52,110 --> 00:17:54,240
Mr. Zhou!

415
00:17:54,640 --> 00:17:55,510
Mr. Zhou!

416
00:17:56,030 --> 00:17:56,720
Mr. Zhou!

417
00:17:57,060 --> 00:17:58,580
-Ke!
-Mr. Zhou!

418
00:17:58,830 --> 00:17:59,510
Ke!

419
00:17:59,790 --> 00:18:01,030
How can you catch up by running?

420
00:18:02,270 --> 00:18:02,710
Ke!

421
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:04,470
Mr. Zhou! What should we do?

422
00:18:05,350 --> 00:18:07,680
The flying rescue backpack I designed

423
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:09,550
can finally come in handy.

424
00:18:16,510 --> 00:18:17,590
Somebody help!

425
00:18:17,590 --> 00:18:18,310
What should we do?

426
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:20,240
Ke!

427
00:18:21,490 --> 00:18:22,220
-Ke!
-I'm coming.

428
00:18:22,390 --> 00:18:22,950
Zhou Ke!

429
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:24,720
Ke!

430
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:27,510
Come down! I'll catch you, Ke!

431
00:18:34,830 --> 00:18:35,480
Ke!

432
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:36,400
Mr. Zhou!

433
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:37,070
Ke!

434
00:18:37,550 --> 00:18:38,480
Mr. Zhou!

435
00:18:39,070 --> 00:18:39,590
Oh my!

436
00:18:41,750 --> 00:18:42,270
Ke!

437
00:18:43,030 --> 00:18:43,750
-Mr. Zhou!
-Ke!

438
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:45,440
Ke!

439
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:46,590
My foot hurts!

440
00:18:49,190 --> 00:18:49,920
Mr. Zhou...

441
00:18:50,510 --> 00:18:51,840
Mr. Zhou is in the sky!

442
00:18:58,720 --> 00:18:59,550
Mr. Zhou!

443
00:18:59,550 --> 00:19:00,360
Ke!

444
00:19:00,390 --> 00:19:01,350
Mr. Zhou!

445
00:19:01,370 --> 00:19:02,850
Help!

446
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:03,590
Here! Here!

447
00:19:03,920 --> 00:19:04,960
Mr. Zhou is up there!

448
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,200
Hold on, Ke!

449
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:10,440
It's getting higher and higher!

450
00:19:13,170 --> 00:19:14,190
[Thirty-Six Stratagems]

451
00:19:14,210 --> 00:19:16,500
[Romance of the Three Kingdoms]

452
00:19:21,440 --> 00:19:22,030
Jiaoqi.

453
00:19:22,030 --> 00:19:22,640
Eat them yourself.

454
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:23,270
Thank you.

455
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:30,350
Zhou Ke and the guys are making a movie.

456
00:19:30,710 --> 00:19:31,950
Shouldn't we sabotage it?

457
00:19:32,400 --> 00:19:33,590
Just that Zhou Ke?

458
00:19:34,960 --> 00:19:36,640
How capable can he be?

459
00:19:37,550 --> 00:19:38,640
Can he fly?

460
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:51,790
Ke!

461
00:19:54,260 --> 00:19:55,070
Don't be afraid!

462
00:19:55,070 --> 00:19:55,980
What should we do?

463
00:19:56,350 --> 00:19:56,750
How...

464
00:19:57,750 --> 00:19:59,160
Use this! Use this!

465
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:05,710
I got it! I got it!

466
00:20:06,310 --> 00:20:07,350
It's getting higher!

467
00:20:08,270 --> 00:20:08,830
We're doomed.

468
00:20:10,030 --> 00:20:11,200
Won't he fall down?

469
00:20:11,510 --> 00:20:12,000
It's fine.

470
00:20:12,020 --> 00:20:12,630
Below him is the sea.

471
00:20:12,750 --> 00:20:13,440
He won't get hurt.

472
00:20:13,750 --> 00:20:14,790
He can't swim.

473
00:20:15,750 --> 00:20:17,110
Ke!

474
00:20:19,400 --> 00:20:20,240
Mr. Zhou!

475
00:20:20,830 --> 00:20:21,640
Ke!

476
00:20:23,350 --> 00:20:24,400
Mr. Zhou!

477
00:20:24,750 --> 00:20:26,310
We'll save you later!

478
00:20:45,550 --> 00:20:46,160
Zhou Ke?

479
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:48,480
Zhou Ke?

480
00:21:32,640 --> 00:21:34,960
-Ke! Ke!
-Mr. Zhou!

481
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:35,960
What should we do?

482
00:21:35,960 --> 00:21:36,680
Mr. Zhou!

483
00:21:37,240 --> 00:21:37,640
Mr. Zhou!

484
00:21:37,640 --> 00:21:38,400
Ke.

485
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:39,480
Give him mouth-to-mouth!

486
00:21:40,750 --> 00:21:43,590
How am I going to explain this to his mom!

487
00:21:46,160 --> 00:21:48,640
Blow harder! Blow harder!

488
00:21:51,410 --> 00:21:53,210
Ke!

489
00:21:55,520 --> 00:21:57,680
Oh my. I'm a bit short of oxygen.

490
00:21:58,680 --> 00:21:59,590
-Let me do it!
-I can't do it anymore!

491
00:21:59,590 --> 00:22:00,200
Come on!

492
00:22:01,070 --> 00:22:02,400
Ke!

493
00:22:03,790 --> 00:22:04,590
Ke!

494
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:35,620
♪ The longest dream I've ever had ♪

495
00:22:35,650 --> 00:22:39,130
♪ Is loving you
while hiding it from the world ♪

496
00:22:39,420 --> 00:22:43,630
♪ Sharing this secret only with myself ♪

497
00:22:44,100 --> 00:22:46,990
♪ It's because I'm not smart ♪

498
00:22:47,380 --> 00:22:50,830
♪ And don't know how to deduce ♪

499
00:22:50,790 --> 00:22:51,590
Zhen?

500
00:22:51,270 --> 00:22:57,910
♪ Figuring out the hidden meaning
when it's too late ♪

501
00:22:58,210 --> 00:23:00,610
♪ The longest dream I've ever had ♪

502
00:23:00,630 --> 00:23:04,050
♪ Is searching for you
all over the world ♪

503
00:23:04,690 --> 00:23:09,340
♪ Following closely like the rhythm
of breathing ♪

504
00:23:09,450 --> 00:23:12,610
♪ You are right there ♪

505
00:23:12,650 --> 00:23:15,620
♪ So intimate ♪

506
00:23:15,650 --> 00:23:19,660
♪ Because fate has brought us here ♪

507
00:23:20,250 --> 00:23:26,160
♪ Slowly scattering into the sky ♪

508
00:23:47,410 --> 00:23:49,220
Good. Very good.

509
00:23:51,700 --> 00:23:53,100
You forced me.

510
00:23:57,480 --> 00:23:59,590
[You all must die]

511
00:24:10,830 --> 00:24:11,480
Help!

512
00:24:12,270 --> 00:24:14,000
Help! Help!

513
00:24:16,350 --> 00:24:16,960
Let me out!

514
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:18,200
Let me out!

515
00:24:21,510 --> 00:24:22,920
Can't you just not work?

516
00:24:23,200 --> 00:24:24,400
Will you support me if I don't?

517
00:24:24,400 --> 00:24:26,000
Okay, I'll support you.

518
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:27,960
I'll support you
for the rest of your life.

519
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:32,960
Stop.

520
00:24:35,510 --> 00:24:36,000
Shengzai,

521
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:37,240
why is Chen Junnan

522
00:24:37,240 --> 00:24:38,160
in your shooting plan?

523
00:24:38,930 --> 00:24:40,650
I'm just trying
to create a horror atmosphere.

524
00:24:41,110 --> 00:24:42,030
I love the suspense dramas on Light On.

525
00:24:42,240 --> 00:24:44,110
If Chen Junnan acts in it,
it would be so perverted.

526
00:24:45,020 --> 00:24:45,980
I don't want to act with him.

527
00:24:46,230 --> 00:24:47,000
So he can't.

528
00:24:47,770 --> 00:24:48,790
I was just giving an example.

529
00:24:49,070 --> 00:24:49,960
If Chen Junnan doesn't work,

530
00:24:50,480 --> 00:24:51,400
Jiahao is fine too.

531
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:54,480
You also think I have a perverted vibe?

532
00:24:55,550 --> 00:24:57,110
What do you think, Mr. Zhou?

533
00:24:58,880 --> 00:24:59,600
First,

534
00:24:59,680 --> 00:25:00,920
I'm just your consultant.

535
00:25:01,240 --> 00:25:02,350
Why am I in it?

536
00:25:02,880 --> 00:25:03,590
Second, didn't we agree

537
00:25:03,590 --> 00:25:04,880
that Shengzai and Yudan would act?

538
00:25:07,070 --> 00:25:07,880
I can act.

539
00:25:08,550 --> 00:25:09,550
But I don't want to do his script.

540
00:25:10,220 --> 00:25:11,270
I want to act in what I like.

541
00:25:17,270 --> 00:25:17,960
Hey!

542
00:25:19,270 --> 00:25:20,510
What's wrong now?

543
00:25:28,140 --> 00:25:29,050
I'll support you!

544
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:39,960
Divine Lord.

545
00:25:41,350 --> 00:25:42,720
You finally said it.

546
00:25:46,920 --> 00:25:49,680
Welcome back, Divine Lord!

547
00:25:50,110 --> 00:25:51,440
Welcome back, Divine Lord.

548
00:25:53,440 --> 00:25:54,310
I am Mo Lihong!

549
00:25:54,310 --> 00:25:55,510
I am Mo Lishou!

550
00:25:55,510 --> 00:25:56,580
I am Mo Lihai!

551
00:25:56,600 --> 00:25:57,640
I am Mo Liqing!

552
00:25:57,670 --> 00:26:00,020
Welcome back, Divine Lord!

553
00:26:00,920 --> 00:26:01,950
Welcome back, Divine Lord.

554
00:26:03,030 --> 00:26:05,680
Divine Lord, you finally said it.

555
00:26:05,680 --> 00:26:06,440
Divine Lord?

556
00:26:07,270 --> 00:26:08,350
What's going on?

557
00:26:08,790 --> 00:26:11,000
You are Divine Lord Tianchou from heaven.

558
00:26:11,160 --> 00:26:12,400
I am Fairy Liuxu.

559
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:14,720
We came down to the mortal world
to undergo a trial.

560
00:26:14,920 --> 00:26:16,790
Only when you say "I'll support you"

561
00:26:17,070 --> 00:26:18,550
can we return to the immortal realm.

562
00:26:19,440 --> 00:26:20,200
It's been nine lifetimes.

563
00:26:20,750 --> 00:26:22,200
You finally said it.

564
00:26:24,370 --> 00:26:25,720
Nine lifetimes?

565
00:26:26,680 --> 00:26:26,920
Stop.

566
00:26:27,350 --> 00:26:28,020
I can't take it anymore.

567
00:26:28,270 --> 00:26:29,070
It's too melodramatic.

568
00:26:29,550 --> 00:26:30,110
What's wrong?

569
00:26:30,130 --> 00:26:31,590
I just like romance dramas on Love On.

570
00:26:32,510 --> 00:26:34,480
You two don't usually
watch the same channel?

571
00:26:35,240 --> 00:26:36,680
We watch TV at different times.

572
00:26:37,070 --> 00:26:38,960
But I like this version.
I want to watch it.

573
00:26:39,590 --> 00:26:40,540
Then I definitely won't act in it.

574
00:26:41,400 --> 00:26:42,140
Suit yourself.

575
00:26:42,200 --> 00:26:42,920
Alright.

576
00:26:43,740 --> 00:26:45,350
Let me share a comedy one.

577
00:26:47,550 --> 00:26:48,000
Hey!

578
00:26:48,790 --> 00:26:49,440
What?

579
00:26:49,750 --> 00:26:50,640
Can't you just not work?

580
00:26:50,960 --> 00:26:52,030
Will you support me if I don't?

581
00:26:52,310 --> 00:26:53,070
I'll support you.

582
00:26:53,130 --> 00:26:54,410
Take care of yourself first.

583
00:26:55,030 --> 00:26:55,920
Idiot.

584
00:27:07,920 --> 00:27:08,920
Cut!

585
00:27:09,090 --> 00:27:10,650
Where did you find this actor?

586
00:27:10,680 --> 00:27:12,680
He won't die
even after being shot so many times.

587
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:13,850
Come on.

588
00:27:13,880 --> 00:27:15,840
My acting philosophy
might be completely different from y—

589
00:27:17,310 --> 00:27:18,240
I designed my act. I...

590
00:27:18,830 --> 00:27:21,000
Juan, your meal is here.

591
00:27:21,000 --> 00:27:21,590
Hello, hello.

592
00:27:21,590 --> 00:27:23,270
Excuse me, is there a box lunch for me?

593
00:27:23,300 --> 00:27:24,580
Are you kidding me?

594
00:27:24,680 --> 00:27:26,070
I've lived for 37 years,

595
00:27:26,310 --> 00:27:27,000
and I've never seen

596
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:28,590
such an unprofessional actor as you!

597
00:27:28,620 --> 00:27:29,870
Get out of here!

598
00:27:30,240 --> 00:27:30,720
Wait a minute.

599
00:27:31,030 --> 00:27:32,640
Are you 37 years old?

600
00:27:33,350 --> 00:27:36,160
I was born on June 22, 1962.

601
00:27:36,160 --> 00:27:36,880
What's wrong?

602
00:27:38,340 --> 00:27:39,420
Get out of here.

603
00:27:40,030 --> 00:27:42,200
You are a puddle of mud.

604
00:27:42,480 --> 00:27:44,750
Your life is cheaper than an ant's.

605
00:27:48,930 --> 00:27:50,790
[Profile: Du Juan]

606
00:28:01,140 --> 00:28:03,160
[Liu Piaopiao]

607
00:28:10,760 --> 00:28:12,650
[Yin Tinchiu]

608
00:28:43,310 --> 00:28:44,110
Where am I?

609
00:28:44,300 --> 00:28:45,350
Mr. Chen Jiahao,

610
00:28:45,610 --> 00:28:47,690
born on June 22, 1962,

611
00:28:48,070 --> 00:28:50,120
suffers from
severe dissociative identity disorder.

612
00:28:50,510 --> 00:28:53,140
We will now perform a lobotomy on you.

613
00:28:54,110 --> 00:28:54,640
No!

614
00:28:55,670 --> 00:28:57,780
I'm not sick! I'm not sick!

615
00:28:58,110 --> 00:28:59,750
Don't go! Don't go!

616
00:29:00,070 --> 00:29:01,550
I don't have
dissociative identity disorder!

617
00:29:01,880 --> 00:29:03,480
We don't have
dissociative identity disorder!

618
00:29:04,510 --> 00:29:06,350
I don't have
dissociative identity disorder!

619
00:29:15,400 --> 00:29:16,510
Excuse me.

620
00:29:16,640 --> 00:29:19,270
What does this have to do with comedy?

621
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:22,030
Humor. Dark humor.

622
00:29:23,070 --> 00:29:24,750
It's quite dark,

623
00:29:24,750 --> 00:29:25,200
but...

624
00:29:26,200 --> 00:29:27,350
Let me tell you

625
00:29:27,720 --> 00:29:29,960
an original story
I've kept hidden for a long time.

626
00:29:32,110 --> 00:29:33,670
[Work Hard]

627
00:30:08,550 --> 00:30:09,440
I think it's pretty good.

628
00:30:10,200 --> 00:30:11,240
Me too.

629
00:30:11,240 --> 00:30:12,000
I also think it's very good.

630
00:30:12,000 --> 00:30:12,880
I think it's excellent!

631
00:30:12,880 --> 00:30:13,800
It's excellent!

632
00:30:13,820 --> 00:30:14,970
Mr. Zhou, what do you think?

633
00:30:17,280 --> 00:30:19,410
I think... What's our budget?

634
00:30:19,900 --> 00:30:20,860
9,527.

635
00:30:21,790 --> 00:30:24,160
That should be enough for half the movie.

636
00:30:25,100 --> 00:30:26,160
Mr. Zhou, when you make a movie,

637
00:30:26,160 --> 00:30:27,640
why do you always need so much money?

638
00:30:27,960 --> 00:30:29,750
Well, his plan requires special effects
from start to finish.

639
00:30:29,770 --> 00:30:30,220
I just...

640
00:30:30,720 --> 00:30:31,400
It's hard to shoot.

641
00:30:32,910 --> 00:30:34,260
We can agree to the demolition.

642
00:30:34,550 --> 00:30:35,510
When the demolition funds come down,

643
00:30:35,510 --> 00:30:36,550
we'll have money to make the movie.

644
00:30:37,080 --> 00:30:37,830
Are you crazy?

645
00:30:37,850 --> 00:30:39,480
We want to make the movie just because

646
00:30:39,720 --> 00:30:40,550
we don't want the demolition.

647
00:30:40,660 --> 00:30:42,100
Jiahao, go to town with me tomorrow

648
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:43,160
to get some Chinese medicine.

649
00:30:43,260 --> 00:30:43,740
I won't take it.

650
00:30:43,850 --> 00:30:45,170
I just couldn't figure it out
for a moment.

651
00:30:45,480 --> 00:30:45,920
Alright.

652
00:30:46,370 --> 00:30:48,130
The first script meeting
for "King of Comedy"

653
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:48,840
is adjourned!

654
00:30:49,310 --> 00:30:51,240
Bye. I need to sell seafood.

655
00:30:55,030 --> 00:30:55,680
Ms. Zhen.

656
00:30:55,700 --> 00:30:56,700
You... you don't need to...

657
00:30:57,030 --> 00:30:57,790
be too anxious.

658
00:30:58,640 --> 00:31:00,160
I'll figure something out for the script.

659
00:31:00,920 --> 00:31:01,920
As for the money,

660
00:31:02,680 --> 00:31:03,680
we'll just take our time.

661
00:31:05,180 --> 00:31:06,580
-Zhen.
-Zhen, you're back?

662
00:31:06,610 --> 00:31:07,790
Zhen is here!

663
00:31:07,790 --> 00:31:08,400
Zhen is here!

664
00:31:08,400 --> 00:31:10,160
Zhen is back!

665
00:31:10,260 --> 00:31:11,220
Zhen is here!

666
00:31:12,830 --> 00:31:14,920
Zhen! You're back?

667
00:31:15,250 --> 00:31:16,840
Don't scam people again.

668
00:31:17,310 --> 00:31:18,030
Yeah.

669
00:31:19,590 --> 00:31:20,680
You scared me to death.

670
00:31:20,680 --> 00:31:21,030
Zhen,

671
00:31:21,240 --> 00:31:23,030
when you asked us to invest before,

672
00:31:23,030 --> 00:31:24,350
none of us did.

673
00:31:24,680 --> 00:31:25,400
On one hand,

674
00:31:25,510 --> 00:31:27,450
there was a mysterious force

675
00:31:27,470 --> 00:31:28,540
stopping us.

676
00:31:29,200 --> 00:31:29,880
On the other hand,

677
00:31:30,270 --> 00:31:31,480
we didn't know

678
00:31:31,720 --> 00:31:34,030
if your project would succeed.

679
00:31:34,240 --> 00:31:34,680
Zhen.

680
00:31:34,840 --> 00:31:36,680
Mr. Sangbiao, I'm Jiahao!

681
00:31:37,750 --> 00:31:38,240
Zhen.

682
00:31:38,350 --> 00:31:39,080
It's okay.

683
00:31:39,310 --> 00:31:40,590
I know your concerns.

684
00:31:40,590 --> 00:31:41,400
I don't blame you.

685
00:31:41,840 --> 00:31:44,650
I saw Mr. Zhou
hanging on the hot air balloon,

686
00:31:44,680 --> 00:31:45,400
risking his life.

687
00:31:45,590 --> 00:31:47,680
The last time I saw someone work so hard

688
00:31:47,680 --> 00:31:48,830
was Jackie Chao.

689
00:31:48,830 --> 00:31:50,200
I love Jackie Chao.

690
00:31:50,360 --> 00:31:51,200
I love Jett Li!

691
00:31:52,200 --> 00:31:53,200
Mr. Zhou.

692
00:31:53,400 --> 00:31:55,720
Even someone who isn't from our village
worked so hard.

693
00:31:55,960 --> 00:31:57,120
How can we, the villagers here,

694
00:31:57,550 --> 00:31:58,880
not support you

695
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:00,250
and just stand by

696
00:32:00,640 --> 00:32:01,550
doing nothing?

697
00:32:01,830 --> 00:32:04,720
-Right!
-Right!

698
00:32:04,720 --> 00:32:05,350
After discussion,

699
00:32:05,400 --> 00:32:06,310
we unanimously decided

700
00:32:06,660 --> 00:32:14,420
to support you!

701
00:32:19,350 --> 00:32:20,640
Thank you all!

702
00:32:21,840 --> 00:32:22,830
Thank you so much

703
00:32:22,830 --> 00:32:24,020
for believing in me

704
00:32:24,590 --> 00:32:25,680
and our team.

705
00:32:27,080 --> 00:32:29,320
I will remember every penny you invested.

706
00:32:29,960 --> 00:32:31,400
We are all investors of this movie.

707
00:32:32,030 --> 00:32:33,480
I will not let you down.

708
00:32:34,200 --> 00:32:35,830
When our village gets better,

709
00:32:36,070 --> 00:32:37,350
we will invest together,

710
00:32:37,680 --> 00:32:38,790
make money together,

711
00:32:39,200 --> 00:32:40,440
and share the dividends together!

712
00:32:41,030 --> 00:32:41,510
Zhen!

713
00:32:42,240 --> 00:32:42,920
What's wrong, Jiahui?

714
00:32:42,920 --> 00:32:43,920
Are we here for dividends?

715
00:32:44,420 --> 00:32:45,660
We watched you grow up!

716
00:32:46,000 --> 00:32:46,880
This is our token of appreciation!

717
00:32:47,310 --> 00:32:48,650
Just consider it our support for you!

718
00:32:48,960 --> 00:32:49,830
We don't want dividends!

719
00:33:04,960 --> 00:33:05,680
Write it down!

720
00:33:05,920 --> 00:33:06,640
Write it down!

721
00:33:06,920 --> 00:33:07,510
Come here, everyone!

722
00:33:07,510 --> 00:33:08,270
Here, here!

723
00:33:08,270 --> 00:33:09,720
Don't push! Don't push!

724
00:33:10,680 --> 00:33:12,000
Line up! Line up!

725
00:33:40,240 --> 00:33:40,680
How much?

726
00:33:46,640 --> 00:33:47,640
How is it?

727
00:33:49,120 --> 00:33:50,320
I lost count again.

728
00:33:52,590 --> 00:33:53,680
How many times have you counted?

729
00:33:53,940 --> 00:33:55,510
Okay, okay, stop counting.

730
00:33:55,930 --> 00:33:58,010
It's 4,056 in total.

731
00:33:58,350 --> 00:33:59,510
2,000 in cash,

732
00:33:59,680 --> 00:34:01,110
200 in daily necessities,

733
00:34:01,200 --> 00:34:03,790
and an IOU for 1,856.

734
00:34:10,800 --> 00:34:13,280
So... are we still making the movie?

735
00:34:14,150 --> 00:34:15,840
Yes. We must.

736
00:34:16,510 --> 00:34:19,030
This money is the villagers' trust in us.

737
00:34:19,150 --> 00:34:20,840
We must make the village better.

738
00:34:21,030 --> 00:34:22,710
We can't let them down.

739
00:34:22,800 --> 00:34:23,190
Right!

740
00:34:24,510 --> 00:34:25,880
We can't let them down.

741
00:34:26,960 --> 00:34:29,800
I totally understand how you feel.

742
00:34:30,110 --> 00:34:31,670
You are very excited, right?

743
00:34:32,780 --> 00:34:35,429
You could say
you're the hope of the whole village.

744
00:34:35,920 --> 00:34:37,400
But the problem now

745
00:34:37,710 --> 00:34:38,880
is right in front of us.

746
00:34:39,110 --> 00:34:40,710
We have no script,

747
00:34:40,760 --> 00:34:42,150
no money,

748
00:34:42,590 --> 00:34:43,880
and no dire—

749
00:34:48,440 --> 00:34:49,760
You could count as a director,

750
00:34:49,780 --> 00:34:51,030
but you haven't shot anything before.

751
00:34:51,030 --> 00:34:52,770
You have no experience, so...

752
00:34:54,300 --> 00:34:55,969
How do we do this?

753
00:34:58,920 --> 00:35:00,840
Don't worry, Sister.

754
00:35:01,280 --> 00:35:01,760
Well...

755
00:35:01,780 --> 00:35:03,740
How about we shoot

756
00:35:03,770 --> 00:35:04,850
with whatever money we have?

757
00:35:05,000 --> 00:35:06,880
We have 2,000,
so let's do it with 2,000 for now!

758
00:35:09,110 --> 00:35:10,150
Worse comes to worst,

759
00:35:10,710 --> 00:35:11,110
I'll shoot it.

760
00:35:13,760 --> 00:35:14,610
I just don't know

761
00:35:15,150 --> 00:35:16,230
if I can handle it.

762
00:35:16,440 --> 00:35:17,320
I'll learn it now.

763
00:35:18,030 --> 00:35:19,070
Sister, don't be like this.

764
00:35:19,070 --> 00:35:19,920
If you are like this...

765
00:35:20,300 --> 00:35:20,690
I...

766
00:35:21,590 --> 00:35:23,550
At worst, we'll let the villagers down

767
00:35:23,880 --> 00:35:25,190
and get kicked out!

768
00:35:25,550 --> 00:35:26,610
We are orphans anyway.

769
00:35:26,790 --> 00:35:27,740
As long as we are together,

770
00:35:27,770 --> 00:35:28,570
anywhere is home,

771
00:35:28,920 --> 00:35:29,440
right?

772
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:34,070
Can I say a few words?

773
00:35:36,710 --> 00:35:37,840
To be honest,

774
00:35:38,670 --> 00:35:40,590
if we want to make a long movie now,

775
00:35:41,380 --> 00:35:43,010
it might not be realistic.

776
00:35:43,880 --> 00:35:44,880
But don't worry.

777
00:35:45,510 --> 00:35:46,480
I still think we can do it.

778
00:35:47,220 --> 00:35:49,010
If we can't make a long movie,
let's make a short one.

779
00:35:49,320 --> 00:35:50,920
It's not meant to be a movie
released in theaters anyway.

780
00:35:50,920 --> 00:35:52,140
Isn't the point
to make the village well-known?

781
00:35:52,630 --> 00:35:53,670
First, money.

782
00:35:54,150 --> 00:35:55,280
I don't think it's a problem.

783
00:35:55,440 --> 00:35:56,630
We can do it
according to how much money we have.

784
00:35:56,890 --> 00:35:58,600
We didn't spend any money
on the things we made before.

785
00:35:58,800 --> 00:35:59,920
We'll use our villagers as actors

786
00:36:00,400 --> 00:36:02,230
and local materials for scenes and props.

787
00:36:02,850 --> 00:36:04,410
We don't have equipment,
so let's shoot with our phones.

788
00:36:04,590 --> 00:36:06,480
Maybe it has an unexpected effect.

789
00:36:06,860 --> 00:36:07,710
Did I say these things

790
00:36:07,710 --> 00:36:08,920
here before?

791
00:36:09,840 --> 00:36:10,480
It doesn't matter.

792
00:36:10,960 --> 00:36:12,550
Second, the script.

793
00:36:12,550 --> 00:36:14,440
The scripts we talked about today

794
00:36:14,920 --> 00:36:15,800
were indeed a bit bold.

795
00:36:16,110 --> 00:36:16,590
It's okay.

796
00:36:16,590 --> 00:36:17,960
I'll help you with it.

797
00:36:18,110 --> 00:36:18,690
I'll take care of it.

798
00:36:19,110 --> 00:36:19,630
Third...

799
00:36:20,710 --> 00:36:21,400
Speaking of the director...

800
00:36:22,480 --> 00:36:24,880
It was indeed partly my fault before.

801
00:36:25,320 --> 00:36:26,800
But later on, this situation...

802
00:36:27,190 --> 00:36:29,920
And Zhen...

803
00:36:31,670 --> 00:36:32,280
doesn't know...

804
00:36:35,440 --> 00:36:36,320
I'll be the director!

805
00:36:38,030 --> 00:36:39,320
Let's hurry up and finish the script

806
00:36:39,920 --> 00:36:40,510
and start shooting immediately.

807
00:36:48,620 --> 00:36:49,680
Is it too late?

808
00:36:53,280 --> 00:36:54,400
Yeah!

809
00:36:55,260 --> 00:36:57,260
Mr. Zhou, I knew you could do it!

810
00:37:08,110 --> 00:37:08,590
Very good!

811
00:37:09,510 --> 00:37:10,840
Great! Great!

812
00:37:11,190 --> 00:37:11,670
How about this?

813
00:37:11,960 --> 00:37:13,150
Let's cook a meal!

814
00:37:13,150 --> 00:37:13,670
Okay.

815
00:37:13,670 --> 00:37:14,840
Let's take it as our kick-off banquet!

816
00:37:14,990 --> 00:37:15,510
Okay!

817
00:37:15,530 --> 00:37:16,420
I'll cook myself!

818
00:37:16,450 --> 00:37:17,250
I'll help you!

819
00:37:26,760 --> 00:37:28,880
Ms. Zhen, well...

820
00:37:29,440 --> 00:37:30,840
So it's not too late for me to come back

821
00:37:30,840 --> 00:37:31,670
and be the director now?

822
00:37:30,890 --> 00:37:34,090
♪ Lost in the crowds, we carry on ♪

823
00:37:32,430 --> 00:37:32,950
Of course.

824
00:37:34,030 --> 00:37:34,510
In that case,

825
00:37:34,180 --> 00:37:37,600
♪ Someone will stay
with you through day and night ♪

826
00:37:34,510 --> 00:37:36,230
will I get paid?

827
00:37:36,230 --> 00:37:37,740
Of course. Don't worry.

828
00:37:37,770 --> 00:37:39,810
Your money is not in that 9,000.

829
00:37:38,560 --> 00:37:41,880
♪ The art of loving and being loved ♪

830
00:37:39,830 --> 00:37:40,980
I've already set it aside for you.

831
00:37:41,710 --> 00:37:43,320
What I mean is...

832
00:37:42,500 --> 00:37:46,100
♪ I'll give my all
to get it right for you ♪

833
00:37:44,480 --> 00:37:45,510
I have a little idea.

834
00:37:46,070 --> 00:37:48,030
Since funds are so tight right now,

835
00:37:47,360 --> 00:37:50,600
♪ Who would risk it all for you? ♪

836
00:37:48,230 --> 00:37:49,190
how about...

837
00:37:49,960 --> 00:37:53,190
I put my money into this?

838
00:37:50,990 --> 00:37:54,180
♪ Locking all the sorrow deep inside ♪

839
00:37:53,480 --> 00:37:53,840
No!

840
00:37:54,600 --> 00:37:58,340
♪ Like a clown who can become ♪

841
00:37:54,920 --> 00:37:56,550
You already agreed to be our director.

842
00:37:56,550 --> 00:37:58,150
We can't take your money.

843
00:37:58,440 --> 00:38:00,280
It's fine. Aren't we short of money now?

844
00:37:59,100 --> 00:38:02,960
♪ The superhero who makes you smile ♪

845
00:38:00,550 --> 00:38:02,880
You can give it to me later
when you have it.

846
00:38:03,510 --> 00:38:04,800
Will your sister agree?

847
00:38:03,920 --> 00:38:06,850
♪ Oh, time ♪

848
00:38:04,880 --> 00:38:06,070
My sister...

849
00:38:06,550 --> 00:38:07,510
Dinner is ready!

850
00:38:06,880 --> 00:38:10,670
♪ People who live like clowns ♪

851
00:38:08,920 --> 00:38:09,670
Let's not tell her.

852
00:38:09,920 --> 00:38:11,190
Use it secretly first.

853
00:38:10,970 --> 00:38:13,850
♪ Have long forgotten the dust
on their sleeves ♪

854
00:38:11,440 --> 00:38:11,920
No need.

855
00:38:11,920 --> 00:38:12,550
I've made up my mind.

856
00:38:12,760 --> 00:38:13,840
I appreciate your kindness.

857
00:38:13,880 --> 00:38:14,400
Thank you.

858
00:38:14,020 --> 00:38:19,350
♪ With honest hearts,
we make this world more tender ♪

859
00:38:16,150 --> 00:38:17,000
Don't thank me.

860
00:38:17,000 --> 00:38:17,880
I should be thanking you.

861
00:38:18,400 --> 00:38:19,190
If you hadn't saved me,

862
00:38:19,190 --> 00:38:21,710
I would have flown over there by now.

863
00:38:19,380 --> 00:38:23,040
♪ Oh, time ♪

864
00:38:22,480 --> 00:38:24,030
Why are you being so polite?

865
00:38:23,250 --> 00:38:27,240
♪ We who were once loved by clowns ♪

866
00:38:24,110 --> 00:38:25,800
If you hadn't been
on that hot air balloon,

867
00:38:26,320 --> 00:38:27,320
the villagers

868
00:38:27,320 --> 00:38:28,710
wouldn't have trusted us so much.

869
00:38:27,740 --> 00:38:30,050
♪ Can become superheroes too ♪

870
00:38:29,110 --> 00:38:29,630
See? That...

871
00:38:30,080 --> 00:38:35,500
♪ Saving every inch of sorrow ♪

872
00:38:30,590 --> 00:38:32,800
Zuxian.
She doesn't love Jackie Chao anymore.

873
00:38:32,840 --> 00:38:33,760
She loves you now.

874
00:38:33,880 --> 00:38:34,320
Anyway,

875
00:38:35,400 --> 00:38:36,030
no matter what,

876
00:38:36,010 --> 00:38:39,870
♪ Then the world is whole again ♪

877
00:38:36,670 --> 00:38:39,320
thank you for saving me.

878
00:38:39,340 --> 00:38:41,170
And thank you for being the director.

879
00:38:41,980 --> 00:38:42,830
You're welcome.

880
00:38:42,850 --> 00:38:43,710
You're welcome.

881
00:38:44,520 --> 00:38:45,570
Then let's eat.

882
00:38:45,600 --> 00:38:46,080
Okay.

883
00:38:46,280 --> 00:38:47,880
Let's go.

884
00:38:51,110 --> 00:38:51,840
Come on.

885
00:38:51,960 --> 00:38:52,840
Come on!

886
00:38:55,150 --> 00:38:56,360
The oil is about ready, right?

887
00:38:56,470 --> 00:38:57,590
-It's ready!
-Put it in!

888
00:39:12,480 --> 00:39:13,400
Director Zhou, you've started working?

889
00:39:15,400 --> 00:39:16,630
Why didn't you make a sound
when you came over?

890
00:39:17,280 --> 00:39:18,800
I'm a doer. What's wrong?

891
00:39:20,230 --> 00:39:23,030
Didn't you say you wouldn't make movies
or direct anymore?

892
00:39:25,430 --> 00:39:28,070
Didn't your reverse psychology

893
00:39:28,070 --> 00:39:28,920
get to me?

894
00:39:29,440 --> 00:39:30,440
You could tell?

895
00:39:30,960 --> 00:39:32,400
You were colluding with them.

896
00:39:32,710 --> 00:39:33,710
If Zhen hadn't said

897
00:39:33,710 --> 00:39:34,710
she'd make me boiled shrimp...

898
00:39:35,470 --> 00:39:36,800
You did this for boiled shrimp?

899
00:39:37,360 --> 00:39:39,800
Mainly to give you a way out.

900
00:39:40,480 --> 00:39:41,360
You were hesitating,

901
00:39:41,360 --> 00:39:42,840
wanting to participate
but embarrassed to say it.

902
00:39:42,840 --> 00:39:43,670
Did you think I couldn't tell?

903
00:39:43,670 --> 00:39:44,550
Go away.

904
00:39:45,510 --> 00:39:46,360
Thank you then.

905
00:39:46,920 --> 00:39:47,800
You're welcome.

906
00:39:59,190 --> 00:40:00,110
-Are you...
-No.

907
00:40:00,440 --> 00:40:01,360
You didn't even know
what I was going to ask,

908
00:40:01,360 --> 00:40:02,280
and you said no.

909
00:40:02,800 --> 00:40:03,760
You gave yourself away.

910
00:40:03,760 --> 00:40:04,760
You were acting guilty.

911
00:40:04,760 --> 00:40:05,880
And you were accusing others
to cover yourself.

912
00:40:07,000 --> 00:40:07,960
Since ancient times,

913
00:40:07,960 --> 00:40:08,840
no one has ever been able

914
00:40:09,370 --> 00:40:11,480
to resist a beautiful woman.

915
00:40:11,600 --> 00:40:12,370
I have to say,

916
00:40:12,400 --> 00:40:13,710
Zhen is indeed quite cute.

917
00:40:13,710 --> 00:40:14,840
Her face, I...

918
00:40:15,870 --> 00:40:16,670
Don't talk nonsense.

919
00:40:18,480 --> 00:40:19,150
Is this the reason?

920
00:40:19,440 --> 00:40:20,280
Is it because of this?

921
00:40:20,710 --> 00:40:21,360
Then why?

922
00:40:21,500 --> 00:40:23,060
You're looking down on me. You know?

923
00:40:23,080 --> 00:40:25,120
I had to step up,
both emotionally and logically.

924
00:40:26,440 --> 00:40:28,030
Okay, then tell me.

925
00:40:29,360 --> 00:40:29,920
Emotionally speaking?

926
00:40:30,480 --> 00:40:31,400
Emotionally speaking...

927
00:40:33,150 --> 00:40:33,880
In the village,

928
00:40:33,880 --> 00:40:34,880
my reputation is so good now.

929
00:40:35,030 --> 00:40:36,150
Talking nonsense, huh?

930
00:40:36,440 --> 00:40:38,150
Look at how much the villagers trust me.

931
00:40:38,150 --> 00:40:39,030
It was so touching.

932
00:40:39,030 --> 00:40:40,150
Would I still be human if I didn't do it?

933
00:40:40,480 --> 00:40:41,230
Logically speaking?

934
00:40:41,630 --> 00:40:43,550
Logically speaking,
they need to make a movie now.

935
00:40:43,550 --> 00:40:44,710
And we happen to know how.

936
00:40:45,400 --> 00:40:46,070
As for yourself?

937
00:40:46,360 --> 00:40:48,440
I've been bursting with a sense of justice
since I was a kid.

938
00:40:49,070 --> 00:40:50,030
As for me?

939
00:40:50,080 --> 00:40:51,040
It can make money.

940
00:40:51,630 --> 00:40:52,480
That's true.

941
00:40:52,800 --> 00:40:54,230
Then as for Zhen?

942
00:40:54,230 --> 00:40:55,110
As for Zhen...

943
00:40:57,630 --> 00:40:59,230
It's still because of Zhen, right?

944
00:40:59,970 --> 00:41:02,220
She's part of the reason, of course.

945
00:41:03,320 --> 00:41:04,710
They offered us money.

946
00:41:05,270 --> 00:41:06,350
And they don't know how to direct.

947
00:41:06,550 --> 00:41:07,550
It's not easy for them.

948
00:41:07,900 --> 00:41:09,650
Most importantly, she saved my life.

949
00:41:10,540 --> 00:41:11,870
That was so brave of her. Otherwise...

950
00:41:13,250 --> 00:41:15,000
And the mouth-to-mouth...

951
00:41:16,550 --> 00:41:17,710
So many people were watching.

952
00:41:19,920 --> 00:41:21,030
Do you like Zhen?

953
00:41:22,600 --> 00:41:23,160
Stop it!

954
00:41:23,190 --> 00:41:24,280
Keep your voice down!

955
00:41:25,110 --> 00:41:25,800
You always talk nonsense!

956
00:41:25,800 --> 00:41:26,550
What if she hears you?

957
00:41:26,840 --> 00:41:27,440
I don't like her!

958
00:41:27,710 --> 00:41:28,800
-You don't like her?
-I don't like her.

959
00:41:28,800 --> 00:41:29,230
Really?

960
00:41:29,230 --> 00:41:30,070
No, I don't like her. I don't like her.

961
00:41:30,070 --> 00:41:30,510
Okay, okay, okay.

962
00:41:30,510 --> 00:41:31,070
It's very simple.

963
00:41:31,190 --> 00:41:32,360
I like her, okay?

964
00:41:32,360 --> 00:41:33,550
I want her to be my sister-in-law.

965
00:41:33,850 --> 00:41:34,560
I want her to be my brother's wife.

966
00:41:35,970 --> 00:41:36,590
Stay out of it.

967
00:41:36,590 --> 00:41:37,140
I'll go ask her.

968
00:41:38,480 --> 00:41:38,960
Are you crazy?

969
00:41:39,070 --> 00:41:39,710
What are you doing?

970
00:41:39,710 --> 00:41:40,880
I'm asking, not you.

971
00:41:40,880 --> 00:41:42,670
I need to ask if she has a boyfriend.

972
00:41:42,670 --> 00:41:43,590
Otherwise, you won't have a chance later.

973
00:41:43,590 --> 00:41:44,110
Right?

974
00:41:44,260 --> 00:41:46,340
I don't plan to be her boyfriend. You...

975
00:41:48,240 --> 00:41:49,070
Remember.

976
00:41:49,840 --> 00:41:52,320
I am the number one Casanova in Shudian.

977
00:41:55,440 --> 00:41:56,800
Just rest assured.

978
00:41:56,800 --> 00:41:57,710
-I'm going!
-Don't be too...

979
00:41:57,730 --> 00:41:59,400
Don't, don't, don't!

980
00:42:01,150 --> 00:42:02,480
Don't ask her too directly!

981
00:42:09,400 --> 00:42:10,070
Please bless me.

982
00:42:11,320 --> 00:42:12,280
Please let it work.

983
00:42:14,190 --> 00:42:14,920
Bless me!

984
00:42:15,000 --> 00:42:15,600
Bless me!

985
00:42:24,480 --> 00:42:26,150
Mouth-to-mouth?

986
00:42:27,230 --> 00:42:28,910
You went too far!
